player:ban(days, hours, minutes, reason [, by]) → boolean
live
Bans the player. The three time parts add up, so ban(0, 1, 30, ...) is 90 minutes and ban(1, 0, 0, ...) is a day. This runs the engine's own ban, so it is indistinguishable from a moderator's: the same server announcement, the same warning notification, the same entry in the player's ban log. The ban is saved with the player and rechecked at login, so it survives a restart and the player is told how long is left when they try to come back. They are disconnected immediately. Returns false when the duration adds up to zero, the reason is empty, or the player is already banned, because the engine never extends or replaces an active punishment. Use player:hasMod(76) to test for one.

days
Whole days. Negative counts as 0, so it can never shorten the total.
hours
Whole hours, added to the days.
minutes
Whole minutes, added to the rest. The total is capped at the engine's own maximum of about 730 days.
reason
Shown to the player and stored on their record. Required: an empty reason is refused.
by
Optional. Who the ban is recorded as coming from, shown in the Punish/View dialog. Defaults to System.
-- auto-ban a player who trips the same warning too often
local strikes = {}

onPlayerCommandCallback(function(world, player, cmd)
    if cmd ~= "/exploit" then return false end

    local id = player:getUserID()
    strikes[id] = (strikes[id] or 0) + 1

    if strikes[id] >= 3 then
        if player:ban(0, 6, 0, "automatic: 3 strikes", "`2AutoMod``") then
            strikes[id] = nil
        end
    else
        player:onConsoleMessage("`4Warning `o(" .. strikes[id] .. "/3)")
    end
    return true
end)
