tile:getVendingCount() → number or nil
live
How many of that item are stocked in the machine.

tile:getVendingPrice() → number or nil
live
The price, whose sign is the selling mode. Above 0 it is World Locks per item: the buyer pays that many locks and gets 1. Below 0 it is items per World Lock: the buyer pays 1 lock and gets that many, so -25 means 25 items for a lock. Exactly 0 means not for sale, and the buyer sees "out of order".

tile:getVendingEarnings() → number or nil
live
World Locks the machine has taken that the owner has not withdrawn yet. Read only. It is banked player money, so only a real purchase and the owner's Withdraw button may move it.

tile:setVending(id, count, price) → bool
live
Stocks a Vending Machine or DigiVend. Applies at once and broadcasts, no world:updateTile needed. count is clamped to the machine's own capacity, 5199 on a Vending Machine and 9999 on a DigiVend. An out of range price is refused outright rather than clamped, because a machine quietly selling at a price you did not ask for is real money. Earnings are never touched. Returns false when the tile is not a vending machine, when id is not a real item, or when the price is out of range.

id
The item to sell, or 0 to empty the machine, which forces count and price to 0 with it.
count
How many to stock. Negative becomes 0, and anything above the machine's capacity is clamped down to it.
price
Above 0, World Locks per item, up to 2000000. Below 0, items per World Lock, magnitude up to 200 and never more than count, so there is always at least one lock's worth in there to buy. 0 takes the machine off sale. Anything outside that is refused and nothing is written.
onPlayerCommandCallback(function(world, player, cmd)
    if cmd ~= "/shop" then return false end

    local t = world:getTile(player:getBlockPosX(), player:getBlockPosY() - 1)
    if not t or not t:getVendingItem() then
        player:onConsoleMessage("`4Stand under a vending machine first.")
        return true
    end

    -- 500 Dirt at 2 World Locks each
    if t:setVending(2, 500, 2) then
        player:onConsoleMessage("`2Machine restocked.")
    else
        player:onConsoleMessage("`4That price was refused.")
    end
    return true
end)
